1
00:00:04,280 --> 00:00:05,800
Hey, you guys ready to order?

2
00:00:05,800 --> 00:00:07,440
- Uh, sure. - Okay, Priya?

3
00:00:07,440 --> 00:00:09,120
Uh, I'll have the shepherd's pie.

4
00:00:09,120 --> 00:00:10,050
You want to split that with me?

5
00:00:10,050 --> 00:00:11,800
Oh, no, no, no, he doesn't.

6
00:00:12,320 --> 00:00:13,240
Why not?

7
00:00:13,240 --> 00:00:14,540
Well, you have milk in the taters,

8
00:00:14,540 --> 00:00:16,520
milk in the gravy, parmesan crust.

9
00:00:16,520 --> 00:00:18,180
Your lactose-intolerant boyfriend will turn

10
00:00:18,180 --> 00:00:21,220
into a gas-filled Macy's Day balloon.

11
00:00:23,280 --> 00:00:24,330
Not quite accurate.

12
00:00:24,330 --> 00:00:26,540
The Macy's balloons are filled with helium,

13
00:00:26,540 --> 00:00:29,870
whereas Leonard produces copious amounts of methane.

14
00:00:34,710 --> 00:00:36,720
So, no, on the shepherd's pie.

15
00:00:36,720 --> 00:00:37,350
Can we move on?

16
00:00:37,350 --> 00:00:39,260
Yeah, a little tip: he says he can eat frozen yogurt.

17
00:00:39,260 --> 00:00:40,990
Do not believe it.

18
00:00:41,770 --> 00:00:43,680
Sea bass! I'll have the sea bass!

19
00:00:44,520 --> 00:00:45,520
You gotta like this,

20
00:00:45,520 --> 00:00:47,880
the girlfriend and the ex-girlfriend bonding

21
00:00:47,880 --> 00:00:50,110
over your rooty-tooty stinky booty.

22
00:00:52,060 --> 00:00:53,140
Kill me.

23
00:00:53,140 --> 00:00:55,550
It wouldn't help. The human body is capable

24
00:00:55,550 --> 00:00:58,260
of being flatulent for hours after death.

25
00:01:02,950 --> 00:01:04,600
Guys, sorry I'm late.

26
00:01:04,600 --> 00:01:05,720
I have amazing news.

27
00:01:05,720 --> 00:01:07,640
Bernadette, before you change the subject,

28
00:01:07,640 --> 00:01:09,490
does anyone have any final comments on

29
00:01:09,490 --> 00:01:12,460
Leonard's faulty digestive system?

30
00:01:12,460 --> 00:01:14,330
So, what's your news, Bernadette?

31
00:01:15,100 --> 00:01:18,120
The thesis committee accepted my doctoral dissertation.

32
00:01:18,120 --> 00:01:19,870
I'm getting my PhD!

33
00:01:19,870 --> 00:01:22,240
Wow! Oh, congratulations.

34
00:01:22,240 --> 00:01:26,980
Wow, so that means you're a doctor, you're a doctor,

35
00:01:26,980 --> 00:01:28,920
you're a doctor, you're a doctor,

36
00:01:28,920 --> 00:01:31,570
and Howard, you know a lot of doctors.

37
00:01:35,460 --> 00:01:37,150
Congratulations, honey.

38
00:01:37,150 --> 00:01:38,070
Thank you.

39
00:01:38,070 --> 00:01:40,300
So, Howard, tell us, how's it feel knowing

40
00:01:40,300 --> 00:01:41,390
that when you two get married,

41
00:01:41,390 --> 00:01:45,080
you'll be referred to as Mr. and Dr. Wolowitz?

42
00:01:45,840 --> 00:01:47,550
Unless he takes Bernadette's last name.

43
00:01:47,550 --> 00:01:49,080
And considering her advanced status,

44
00:01:49,080 --> 00:01:51,250
that could open some doors for him.

45
00:01:51,250 --> 00:01:53,010
Please, this isn't about me.

46
00:01:53,010 --> 00:01:54,500
I'm proud of you.

47
00:01:54,500 --> 00:01:56,230
Well, you'll be really be proud of this.

48
00:01:56,230 --> 00:01:59,130
I was headhunted by a big pharmaceutical company.

49
00:01:59,130 --> 00:02:01,970
They're gonna pay me a buttload of money!

50
00:02:01,970 --> 00:02:03,070
What?

51
00:02:03,070 --> 00:02:05,010
Bernadette, that's great.

52
00:02:05,010 --> 00:02:07,110
Howard, do you make a buttload?

53
00:02:07,920 --> 00:02:10,440
Better than what you've got a buttload of.

54
00:02:13,520 --> 00:02:16,120
Hey, if I roll down the windows in the car, everything's peachy.

55
00:02:16,120 --> 00:02:18,540
If you do it, you're still not a doctor.

56
00:02:19,550 --> 00:02:21,510
Yeah, just a heads-up on the car window deal.

57
00:02:21,510 --> 00:02:24,770
It helps, but everything is not "peachy."

58
00:02:51,220 --> 00:02:53,330
*Oh, if there was a problem, you can't solve it*

59
00:02:53,330 --> 00:02:55,380
*Check out the hook while my DJ revolves it*

60
00:02:55,380 --> 00:02:58,380
*Ice, Ice, baby*

61
00:02:59,380 --> 00:03:01,810
*Ice, Ice, baby*

62
00:03:03,690 --> 00:03:07,070
Oh, God, I feel ridiculous in this dress.

63
00:03:07,070 --> 00:03:09,560
You look beautiful, Lieutenant Uhura.

64
00:03:10,660 --> 00:03:14,080
Now prepare for... inspection.

65
00:03:15,140 --> 00:03:17,300
Shh, my brother's going to hear you.

66
00:03:17,300 --> 00:03:19,010
Relax, he's got headphones on.

67
00:03:19,010 --> 00:03:22,100
And we're ten miles above Earth in a starship.

68
00:03:22,580 --> 00:03:24,000
Really, ten miles?

69
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:26,340
You're orbiting inside the atmosphere?

70
00:03:26,980 --> 00:03:28,460
Moron.

71
00:03:28,460 --> 00:03:32,100
I can't believe I'm wearing my brother's Halloween costume.

72
00:03:33,180 --> 00:03:35,940
I can't believe you think he only wears it on Halloween.

73
00:03:37,110 --> 00:03:40,360
Open the landing bay doors, shuttle craft approaching.

74
00:03:40,360 --> 00:03:42,290
Okay, gotta go.

75
00:03:48,710 --> 00:03:50,090
Hey, what's up?

76
00:03:50,090 --> 00:03:54,460
Is that my future daughter-in-law, the doctor?!

77
00:03:56,190 --> 00:03:58,610
No, Ma! It's Raj!

78
00:03:58,610 --> 00:04:02,150
- He's a doctor too, right?! - Yes!

79
00:04:02,150 --> 00:04:05,060
Like Leonard and the skinny weirdo!

80
00:04:07,760 --> 00:04:08,850
Sheldon, yes!

81
00:04:08,850 --> 00:04:11,380
Everybody's a doctor but me!

82
00:04:11,380 --> 00:04:13,960
Well, whose fault is that?!

83
00:04:16,400 --> 00:04:17,840
What's up?

84
00:04:18,210 --> 00:04:19,530
Leonard's putting disgusting memories in

85
00:04:19,530 --> 00:04:21,960
my memory foam mattress.

86
00:04:22,810 --> 00:04:24,900
Can I stay here tonight?

87
00:04:24,900 --> 00:04:26,780
Sure, but I'm going out with Bernadette.

88
00:04:26,780 --> 00:04:28,740
It'll just be you and my mother.

89
00:04:28,740 --> 00:04:30,150
I guess that's okay.

90
00:04:30,150 --> 00:04:32,780
Ma, can Rajesh sleep over?!

91
00:04:32,780 --> 00:04:36,990
Of course, he and I can play doctor!

92
00:04:40,560 --> 00:04:42,100
She's kidding, right?

93
00:04:42,100 --> 00:04:43,750
I don't know, she's pretty feisty since

94
00:04:43,750 --> 00:04:46,780
they put her on hormone-replacement therapy.

95
00:04:48,010 --> 00:04:51,650
Paging Dr. Cutie Pie!

96
00:04:54,240 --> 00:04:56,610
I must say, Amy, I was very impressed

97
00:04:56,610 --> 00:04:58,940
to see that Bernadette got her PhD.

98
00:04:58,940 --> 00:05:00,390
It's indeed admirable.

99
00:05:00,390 --> 00:05:02,910
Although, it is... microbiology.

100
00:05:04,430 --> 00:05:07,090
Your doctorate is in neurobiology.

101
00:05:07,090 --> 00:05:08,780
I fail to see the distinction.

102
00:05:08,780 --> 00:05:10,350
I'll make it simple for you.

103
00:05:10,350 --> 00:05:11,670
I study the brain,

104
00:05:11,670 --> 00:05:14,230
the organ responsible for Beethoven's Fifth Symphony.

105
00:05:14,230 --> 00:05:15,640
Bernadette studies yeast,

106
00:05:15,640 --> 00:05:18,450
the organism responsible for Michelob Lite.

107
00:05:20,660 --> 00:05:22,260
Is there something wrong with your neck?

108
00:05:22,260 --> 00:05:24,230
It's a little stiff.

109
00:05:24,230 --> 00:05:26,290
What a remarkably fragile structure

110
00:05:26,290 --> 00:05:28,900
to support such a valuable payload.

111
00:05:30,490 --> 00:05:34,380
Not unlike balancing a Faberge egg on a Pixie Stick.

112
00:05:35,030 --> 00:05:36,870
Have you considered massage?

113
00:05:36,870 --> 00:05:39,150
I'd like to respond to that sarcastically:

114
00:05:39,150 --> 00:05:42,220
Yes, I relish the thought of a stranger covering my body

115
00:05:42,220 --> 00:05:44,260
with oil and rubbing it.

116
00:05:45,540 --> 00:05:49,130
I was proposing you massage your muscles with your own hands.

117
00:05:49,130 --> 00:05:51,760
Still sounds like a lot of unnecessary touching.

118
00:05:52,390 --> 00:05:53,670
Trust me.

119
00:05:53,670 --> 00:05:54,690
With your right hand,

120
00:05:54,690 --> 00:05:58,370
locate the spot where the scapula meets the acromion process.

121
00:06:00,190 --> 00:06:00,930
All right.

122
00:06:00,930 --> 00:06:03,610
Now push your third finger along the ridge of the shoulder blade,

123
00:06:03,610 --> 00:06:06,230
making a small rotation as you do so.

124
00:06:07,330 --> 00:06:08,640
Rotating.

125
00:06:09,190 --> 00:06:11,030
You should feel a small node-like object

126
00:06:11,030 --> 00:06:13,420
rolling back and forth along the bone.

127
00:06:13,420 --> 00:06:15,050
You mean the myofascial point?

128
00:06:15,050 --> 00:06:16,520
Obviously.

129
00:06:18,110 --> 00:06:19,410
Now bear down on it

130
00:06:19,410 --> 00:06:20,590
like the seventh grade noogies

131
00:06:20,590 --> 00:06:22,300
we all know too well.

132
00:06:24,260 --> 00:06:29,660
Oh, dear Lord, yes, yes, oh, yes!

133
00:06:30,180 --> 00:06:32,930
Amy, I've never been touched like this before!

134
00:06:35,070 --> 00:06:37,510
Oh! My hands are magic!

135
00:06:38,560 --> 00:06:39,900
Don't flatter yourself.

136
00:06:39,900 --> 00:06:42,250
Your hands are blunt tools guided by my knowledge

137
00:06:42,250 --> 00:06:43,930
of the nervous system.

138
00:06:44,340 --> 00:06:46,520
I could just as easily have paralyzed you.

139
00:06:49,400 --> 00:06:51,060
There's someone at my door.

140
00:06:51,060 --> 00:06:53,210
That doesn't interest me. Good-bye.

141
00:06:58,700 --> 00:07:00,680
- Can I sleep here tonight? - Why?

142
00:07:00,680 --> 00:07:02,410
Leonard's having astronomically inaccurate

143
00:07:02,410 --> 00:07:04,730
Star Trek sex with my sister.

144
00:07:05,770 --> 00:07:08,250
I can see how that would be upsetting. Come in.

145
00:07:09,170 --> 00:07:11,220
I'll get the sheets and blankets for the couch.

146
00:07:11,220 --> 00:07:13,200
Oh, don't bother. I'll just sleep in Leonard's room.

147
00:07:13,200 --> 00:07:15,970
No, I can't authorize that.

148
00:07:15,970 --> 00:07:18,030
Well, he's in my bed. Why can't I be in his?

149
00:07:18,320 --> 00:07:20,800
The Hammurabic Code is "an eye for an eye,"

150
00:07:20,800 --> 00:07:22,390
not "a bed for a bed."

151
00:07:22,830 --> 00:07:24,580
Come on, dude, I'm exhausted,

152
00:07:24,580 --> 00:07:25,400
and Tyra Banks says

153
00:07:25,400 --> 00:07:27,070
the most important item in your makeup bag

154
00:07:27,070 --> 00:07:28,560
is a good night's sleep.

155
00:07:32,850 --> 00:07:34,040
All right.

156
00:07:34,040 --> 00:07:37,800
This is a form indemnifying me

157
00:07:37,800 --> 00:07:41,900
from your use of "Leonard's bedroom."

158
00:07:41,900 --> 00:07:44,400
Sign here, indicating that I tried to stop you

159
00:07:44,400 --> 00:07:47,430
and did so using a stern facial expression.

160
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:54,360
- Good night, Sheldon.  - Wait. Not yet.

161
00:07:54,360 --> 00:07:56,020
We still have to go over safety procedures.

162
00:07:56,020 --> 00:07:59,220
Now, the apartment has three emergency exits located

163
00:07:59,220 --> 00:08:02,030
here, here, and here.

164
00:08:02,030 --> 00:08:03,610
In the event of a power outage,

165
00:08:03,610 --> 00:08:06,830
luminous paint will guide you to the nearest exit.

166
00:08:07,390 --> 00:08:08,580
You're kidding.

167
00:08:18,520 --> 00:08:20,580
I never kid about safety.

168
00:08:33,720 --> 00:08:35,210
What are you doing here?

169
00:08:35,210 --> 00:08:36,300
I was sleeping.

170
00:08:36,300 --> 00:08:37,280
In my bed?

171
00:08:37,280 --> 00:08:38,620
Well, I would've slept in my own bed,

172
00:08:38,620 --> 00:08:41,300
but it was being used to bring shame to my family.

173
00:08:43,010 --> 00:08:45,380
And the memory of Gene Roddenberry.

174
00:08:46,830 --> 00:08:47,690
Oh, you heard?

175
00:08:47,690 --> 00:08:50,640
"Scotty, I need more power."

176
00:08:52,380 --> 00:08:54,910
Sorry. Does Sheldon know you're sleeping in here?

177
00:08:54,910 --> 00:08:56,850
Are you kidding? He made me sign a waiver,

178
00:08:56,850 --> 00:08:58,970
participate in an emergency fire drill

179
00:08:58,970 --> 00:09:01,750
and take a refresher course in CPR.

180
00:09:02,350 --> 00:09:04,210
Thank God he had a dummy.

181
00:09:04,860 --> 00:09:07,080
Oh, yeah. Mouth-to-Mouth Mona.

182
00:09:08,660 --> 00:09:10,580
You know, she used to date Howard?

183
00:09:11,470 --> 00:09:13,640
Oh, my God, she's that Mona?

184
00:09:15,460 --> 00:09:17,350
Why can't you and my sister spend your nights here?

185
00:09:17,350 --> 00:09:19,490
We tried. She doesn't get along with Sheldon.

186
00:09:19,490 --> 00:09:21,940
Sheldon doesn't get along with Sheldon.

187
00:09:22,780 --> 00:09:24,410
It's still no reason for me to have to listen to you

188
00:09:24,410 --> 00:09:27,330
arm your photon torpedoes every night.

189
00:09:28,180 --> 00:09:29,260
Okay, well, how about this:

190
00:09:29,260 --> 00:09:30,930
until Priya gets her own place,

191
00:09:30,930 --> 00:09:33,510
you stay here and I'll stay at your apartment.

192
00:09:34,750 --> 00:09:37,350
Can I bring girls here?

193
00:09:37,350 --> 00:09:38,720
You?

194
00:09:39,560 --> 00:09:41,980
Sure. Bring as many as you want.

195
00:09:43,220 --> 00:09:44,700
Okay, deal.

196
00:09:46,340 --> 00:09:48,410
Just not against their will.

197
00:09:54,270 --> 00:09:56,410
You really think you should be eating that cake?

198
00:09:56,410 --> 00:09:57,480
Why?

199
00:09:57,480 --> 00:09:59,370
If you're gonna be a trophy husband for a rich wife,

200
00:09:59,370 --> 00:10:01,420
you might want to watch your waistline.

201
00:10:02,650 --> 00:10:03,490
He's right.

202
00:10:03,490 --> 00:10:06,560
A minute on the lips, a lifetime on the hips.

203
00:10:07,330 --> 00:10:08,730
Yeah, ha-ha.

204
00:10:08,730 --> 00:10:12,030
First of all, I'm not threatened by my fiance's success.

205
00:10:12,030 --> 00:10:12,970
I'm proud of her.

206
00:10:12,970 --> 00:10:15,720
And secondly, I have my own career.

207
00:10:16,240 --> 00:10:18,450
Until you have kids.

208
00:10:19,380 --> 00:10:20,830
Good news, Raj.

209
00:10:20,830 --> 00:10:22,990
I got the blood work back from the lab.

210
00:10:22,990 --> 00:10:25,140
You're okay to stay for a while.

211
00:10:25,720 --> 00:10:27,310
When did you take my blood?

212
00:10:27,310 --> 00:10:28,850
Not important.

213
00:10:30,140 --> 00:10:31,960
Your sugar was a little high.

214
00:10:31,960 --> 00:10:34,350
I'd follow up with your regular physician.

215
00:10:34,350 --> 00:10:36,560
In the meantime, I have some paperwork here

216
00:10:36,560 --> 00:10:37,840
for you to go over.

217
00:10:37,840 --> 00:10:38,690
What the hell is this?

218
00:10:38,690 --> 00:10:40,250
Boilerplate stuff.

219
00:10:40,250 --> 00:10:43,440
A modified roommate agreement for a temporary house guest.

220
00:10:43,440 --> 00:10:46,870
And a living will and durable power of attorney.

221
00:10:48,090 --> 00:10:52,410
This says you can make "end of life" decisions for me.

222
00:10:52,410 --> 00:10:55,450
As your friend, let's hope it doesn't come to that.

223
00:10:55,450 --> 00:10:57,110
Please sign.

224
00:10:57,110 --> 00:10:58,290
Did you sign this?

225
00:10:58,290 --> 00:10:59,720
There's a reciprocity clause.

226
00:10:59,720 --> 00:11:01,830
You get to pull the plug on him, too.

227
00:11:03,010 --> 00:11:04,530
Well, that seems fair.

228
00:11:06,450 --> 00:11:09,100
Congratulations and welcome temporarily aboard.

229
00:11:09,100 --> 00:11:11,800
Here's your I.D. card,

230
00:11:11,800 --> 00:11:15,520
your key and your lapel pin.

231
00:11:15,520 --> 00:11:18,900
Which Leonard was too cool to wear.

232
00:11:22,080 --> 00:11:25,440
FYI, part of your responsibilities as roommate pro tem

233
00:11:25,440 --> 00:11:27,410
will be to drive me to and from work,

234
00:11:27,410 --> 00:11:29,690
the comic book store, the barbershop

235
00:11:29,690 --> 00:11:33,760
and the park for one hour every other Sunday for fresh air.

236
00:11:35,230 --> 00:11:36,650
Bring a ball or a Frisbee,

237
00:11:36,650 --> 00:11:38,750
you know, something he can chase.

238
00:11:40,680 --> 00:11:43,520
Also, you're tasked with bringing home all takeout dinners.

239
00:11:43,520 --> 00:11:44,790
Tonight is Thai food.

240
00:11:44,790 --> 00:11:47,140
You'll find the standard order in appendix B

241
00:11:47,140 --> 00:11:49,780
or downloadable from my FTP server.

242
00:11:49,780 --> 00:11:51,190
If you have any questions,

243
00:11:51,190 --> 00:11:52,860
here's the FAQ sheet,

244
00:11:52,860 --> 00:11:54,790
or if you prefer the human touch,

245
00:11:54,790 --> 00:11:58,890
I do a live web chat called "Apartment Talk" on Tuesday nights

246
00:12:01,600 --> 00:12:03,740
No backsies.

247
00:12:08,940 --> 00:12:11,450
Sheldon, dinner!

248
00:12:18,430 --> 00:12:20,420
What is this?

249
00:12:20,420 --> 00:12:25,270
This is the difference between eating and dining.

250
00:12:27,580 --> 00:12:31,620
Remarkable. I'm just realizing how much

251
00:12:31,620 --> 00:12:35,080
Leonard's been skating by all these years.

252
00:12:36,100 --> 00:12:37,410
It's not a big thing.

253
00:12:37,410 --> 00:12:40,190
Just think of me as a brown Martha Stewart.

254
00:12:42,730 --> 00:12:43,580
Hey, Sheldon,

255
00:12:43,580 --> 00:12:45,540
did you change your Wi-Fi password again?

256
00:12:45,540 --> 00:12:48,960
Yes, it's "Penny, get your own Wi-Fi." No spaces.

257
00:12:50,030 --> 00:12:51,010
Thanks.

258
00:12:51,010 --> 00:12:53,210
What's with the fancy spread?

259
00:12:53,210 --> 00:12:55,450
My new roommate is bending over backwards

260
00:12:55,450 --> 00:12:57,470
to ingratiate himself to me.

261
00:12:57,470 --> 00:12:59,750
Uh, nice touch, by the way.

262
00:13:01,930 --> 00:13:03,930
What do you mean "new roommate"? What happened to Leonard?

263
00:13:03,930 --> 00:13:05,970
The same thing that happened to Homo erectus.

264
00:13:05,970 --> 00:13:08,940
He was replaced by a superior species.

265
00:13:10,040 --> 00:13:12,580
I'm the new Homo in town.

266
00:13:15,600 --> 00:13:17,780
That came out wrong.

267
00:13:17,780 --> 00:13:19,820
All right, let me try this again. Where's Leonard?

268
00:13:19,820 --> 00:13:22,150
He's living at my place, so I'm living here.

269
00:13:22,150 --> 00:13:24,340
You're living here provisionally.

270
00:13:24,340 --> 00:13:26,750
But I must say it's looking good.

271
00:13:27,680 --> 00:13:29,670
Leonard and Priya are living together?

272
00:13:29,670 --> 00:13:30,520
That's big.

273
00:13:30,520 --> 00:13:33,990
No. Origami napkin swans...

274
00:13:36,200 --> 00:13:38,620
that's the headline.

275
00:13:39,280 --> 00:13:41,480
It's a good thing.

276
00:13:43,260 --> 00:13:45,700
So do you know what kind of research you'll be doing

277
00:13:45,700 --> 00:13:47,550
at this pharmaceutical company?

278
00:13:47,550 --> 00:13:50,070
Well, there are a couple of opportunities available,

279
00:13:50,070 --> 00:13:54,160
but I volunteered for the premature ejaculation project.

280
00:13:58,690 --> 00:14:02,370
I mean, it's not like either one of us has heart disease.

281
00:14:06,250 --> 00:14:08,730
Oh, I almost forgot. I got you a little present.

282
00:14:08,730 --> 00:14:11,290
Oh, Bernie, no. You didn't have to.

283
00:14:11,290 --> 00:14:13,540
I wanted to. Come on, open it.

284
00:14:16,950 --> 00:14:20,110
You bought me a Rolex?

285
00:14:20,110 --> 00:14:22,440
How much did this cost?

286
00:14:22,440 --> 00:14:25,220
Oh, you let me worry about the money.

287
00:14:27,380 --> 00:14:30,710
I just want my baby to have pretty things.

288
00:14:34,940 --> 00:14:36,080
More wine?

289
00:14:36,080 --> 00:14:38,170
Oh, no, no, no. I've had way too much already.

290
00:14:38,170 --> 00:14:40,590
Here's an interesting fact about alcohol...

291
00:14:40,590 --> 00:14:42,340
Hit me.

292
00:14:45,720 --> 00:14:48,020
Man is not the only species

293
00:14:48,020 --> 00:14:51,190
that ferments fruit in order to become intoxicated.

294
00:14:51,190 --> 00:14:52,900
Can you guess what the other is?

295
00:14:52,900 --> 00:14:58,410
Hint: sometimes they pack the alcohol in their trunks.

296
00:14:58,410 --> 00:15:00,400
Monkeys.

297
00:15:03,350 --> 00:15:06,350
When does a monkey have a trunk?

298
00:15:06,350 --> 00:15:09,150
When a suitcase just won't do.

299
00:15:12,320 --> 00:15:14,500
Mmm, all right.

300
00:15:14,500 --> 00:15:16,190
It would appear as if alcohol

301
00:15:16,190 --> 00:15:19,210
is playing keep-away with your intelligence.

302
00:15:19,210 --> 00:15:20,580
Good night.

303
00:15:20,580 --> 00:15:22,880
Please note, it is now past 10:00 p.m.

304
00:15:22,880 --> 00:15:25,130
Per our roommate agreement, kindly refrain

305
00:15:25,130 --> 00:15:26,420
from raucous laughter,

306
00:15:26,420 --> 00:15:30,400
clinking of glasses, and celebratory gunfire.

307
00:15:32,590 --> 00:15:33,830
Okay...

308
00:15:33,830 --> 00:15:35,790
explain something to me.

309
00:15:35,790 --> 00:15:39,390
You watch Leonard put up with that guy for years and years.

310
00:15:39,390 --> 00:15:42,170
What has to break inside your brain for you to think,

311
00:15:42,170 --> 00:15:45,170
"Oh, Krishna, I've got to get me some of that"?

312
00:15:46,580 --> 00:15:48,310
Well, it's a lot better than having

313
00:15:48,310 --> 00:15:50,830
to wear noise-cancelling headphones in my own apartment.

314
00:15:50,830 --> 00:15:52,870
What? Oh, God, yeah. Yeah.

315
00:15:52,870 --> 00:15:55,400
Leonard's a noisy little dude in the sack.

316
00:15:55,810 --> 00:15:57,530
- Every night. - Really?

317
00:15:57,530 --> 00:15:59,540
Even during allergy season, when he has to alternate

318
00:15:59,540 --> 00:16:01,570
between kissing and breathing?

319
00:16:03,750 --> 00:16:06,110
It's my sister. Can we not talk about this anymore?

320
00:16:06,110 --> 00:16:07,810
Yeah. Sorry, sorry.

321
00:16:10,200 --> 00:16:11,390
Can I tell you a secret?

322
00:16:11,390 --> 00:16:13,370
Yeah.

323
00:16:13,370 --> 00:16:15,040
I screwed up.

324
00:16:15,040 --> 00:16:16,160
Leonard's a great guy.

325
00:16:16,160 --> 00:16:18,470
Never should have broken up with him.

326
00:16:19,960 --> 00:16:22,510
Well, uh, to paraphrase Shakespeare:

327
00:16:22,510 --> 00:16:24,680
"It's better to have loved and lost

328
00:16:24,680 --> 00:16:25,840
"than to stay home every night

329
00:16:25,840 --> 00:16:28,920
and download increasingly shameful pornography."

330
00:16:31,990 --> 00:16:35,570
Ohh... you poor baby.

331
00:16:35,570 --> 00:16:36,710
What's wrong with me, Penny?

332
00:16:36,710 --> 00:16:38,100
Nothing, nothing.

333
00:16:38,100 --> 00:16:39,620
You know, if we weren't friends,

334
00:16:39,620 --> 00:16:43,010
and you hadn't brought up that creepy pornography story,

335
00:16:43,010 --> 00:16:43,750
I'd be on you like

336
00:16:43,750 --> 00:16:46,950
the speed of light squared on matter to make energy.

337
00:16:47,340 --> 00:16:48,890
Hey, you totally got that right!

338
00:16:48,890 --> 00:16:50,550
"E=mc2."

339
00:16:50,550 --> 00:16:51,560
I listen.

340
00:16:51,560 --> 00:16:54,030
I have no idea what it means, but I listen.

341
00:16:55,840 --> 00:16:58,550
- To friendship. - To friendship.

342
00:16:59,270 --> 00:17:02,750
Would you booze hounds please stop that infernal clinking?!

343
00:17:05,360 --> 00:17:07,750
And the answer was elephant!

344
00:17:15,860 --> 00:17:16,780
Leonard, sweetheart,

345
00:17:16,780 --> 00:17:19,360
we're kissing, not eating hot soup.

346
00:17:20,750 --> 00:17:21,990
Sorry.

347
00:17:26,420 --> 00:17:28,490
That's my parents on video chat.

348
00:17:28,490 --> 00:17:29,540
Go hide in the bedroom.

349
00:17:29,540 --> 00:17:30,410
Oh, come on!

350
00:17:30,410 --> 00:17:32,590
Why don't we just tell them that we're dating?

351
00:17:32,590 --> 00:17:34,240
Oh, we've been through this. It's not the time.

352
00:17:34,240 --> 00:17:35,340
When is the time?

353
00:17:35,340 --> 00:17:36,710
I've got five brothers and sisters.

354
00:17:36,710 --> 00:17:38,380
One of them is bound to screw up real big,

355
00:17:38,380 --> 00:17:40,230
and then I'll tell my parents about you.

356
00:17:40,230 --> 00:17:41,850
- Now, shoo. - Fine.

357
00:17:44,780 --> 00:17:46,730
Hello, Mummy. Hello, Daddy.

358
00:17:46,730 --> 00:17:48,340
We heard there was a tornado in Kansas City.

359
00:17:48,340 --> 00:17:50,630
Is that close to you?

360
00:17:51,350 --> 00:17:52,190
No.

361
00:17:52,190 --> 00:17:53,700
Where is your brother?

362
00:17:53,700 --> 00:17:55,010
Out with friends.

363
00:17:55,010 --> 00:17:57,460
I don't like it, a young girl alone in an apartment.

364
00:17:57,460 --> 00:17:58,410
I'll sleep so much better

365
00:17:58,410 --> 00:18:00,230
when you move back here next month.

366
00:18:00,230 --> 00:18:02,500
You're moving back to India?!

367
00:18:02,500 --> 00:18:03,210
Who's that?

368
00:18:03,210 --> 00:18:05,310
Oh, my God! There's someone in your apartment.

369
00:18:05,310 --> 00:18:07,380
Call the police in America!

370
00:18:07,380 --> 00:18:09,530
When were you going to tell me about this?

371
00:18:09,530 --> 00:18:11,220
Oh, hello, Leonard.

372
00:18:11,220 --> 00:18:12,970
What a pleasant surprise!

373
00:18:12,970 --> 00:18:16,530
Mummy, Daddy, you remember Rajesh's friend Leonard.

374
00:18:16,530 --> 00:18:19,050
I thought you said Rajesh was out with his friends.

375
00:18:19,050 --> 00:18:21,020
He has many friends.

376
00:18:21,020 --> 00:18:23,190
Rajesh has many friends?

377
00:18:24,160 --> 00:18:26,600
Why are you lying to us?

378
00:18:26,830 --> 00:18:28,260
She's lying because she doesn't want you to know

379
00:18:28,260 --> 00:18:29,600
- we're dating. - Leonard!

380
00:18:29,600 --> 00:18:30,430
Well, what difference does it make?

381
00:18:30,430 --> 00:18:33,970
If you're moving back to India, we're obviously breaking up.

382
00:18:34,430 --> 00:18:38,020
You know what? I don't want to deal with this right now.

383
00:18:45,310 --> 00:18:47,330
So...

384
00:18:47,330 --> 00:18:49,300
Hot in India?

385
00:18:50,170 --> 00:18:52,790
Of course it is. It always is. It's India.

386
00:18:54,700 --> 00:18:57,060
Now, what do you have to say for yourself?

387
00:18:58,760 --> 00:19:02,010
That is a beautiful tapestry.

388
00:19:35,320 --> 00:19:37,430
Oh, God.

389
00:19:42,530 --> 00:19:44,220
Oh, God!

390
00:19:47,580 --> 00:19:48,770
Okay, look.

391
00:19:48,770 --> 00:19:51,010
This never happened.

392
00:19:51,010 --> 00:19:52,680
Do you understand me?

393
00:19:55,370 --> 00:19:57,630
Really?! Still can't talk to me?

394
00:20:01,140 --> 00:20:03,240
What are you doing here?

395
00:20:03,240 --> 00:20:03,880
What?

396
00:20:03,880 --> 00:20:05,720
I said, what are you doing here?

397
00:20:05,720 --> 00:20:07,770
I live here.

398
00:20:07,770 --> 00:20:10,390
I have paperwork that says differently.

399
00:20:13,030 --> 00:20:15,140
Priya's going back to India.

400
00:20:15,140 --> 00:20:17,320
Irrelevant.

401
00:20:17,320 --> 00:20:18,660
Rajesh and I have a good thing going

402
00:20:18,660 --> 00:20:20,850
and you're not going to ruin it.

403
00:20:24,490 --> 00:20:26,850
What are you doing here?

404
00:20:26,850 --> 00:20:27,530
I've been up all night.

405
00:20:27,530 --> 00:20:30,640
- I had a fight with Bernadette. - Why?

406
00:20:30,640 --> 00:20:33,430
She gave me a beautiful watch.

407
00:20:35,880 --> 00:20:37,950
Leonard, do you understand this?

408
00:20:38,390 --> 00:20:39,400
Yes.

409
00:20:39,400 --> 00:20:40,960
Talk to him.

410
00:20:50,150 --> 00:20:51,730
Damn.

411
00:20:52,880 --> 00:20:54,570
What's going on?

412
00:20:56,390 --> 00:20:58,670
It's-it's not what it looks like.

413
00:21:02,330 --> 00:21:04,530
What does it look like?

